---
title: "statechart.py: one run of the command"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Breaks OutputOnlyOnSuccess in some cases
    lg1: Path to the FoldersGoAfterCommand or OutputOnlyOnSuccess or TLCStopsAfterCommand bug
    lg2: Repeats forever, so FoldersGoAfterCommand or TLCStopsAfterCommand breaks
  }
  class lg0 mayBreak
  class lg1 bugPath
  class lg2 repeats
  state "The command is alive" as s0 {
    s1: The command starts the worker, which runs TLC
    s2: The command removes its folders
    s3: The command starts the janitor process
    s4: The command waits for TLC to finish
    s5: The command reads TLC's exit code
    s6: The command moves the chart and report into --out
    s7: The command prints the report to stdout
    [*] --> s1
  }
  s8: The command is dead, and the janitor and TLC may still run
  s9: The command has removed its folders and exited
  [*] --> s0
  s1 --> s2: the worker fails to start
  s1 --> s1: the program that reads stdout exits (as with | head) or you press Ctrl-C
  s1 --> s3: the worker starts and runs TLC
  s2 --> s9: the folders are gone and the command exits
  s3 --> s2: the janitor process fails to start
  s3 --> s4: the janitor process starts
  s3 --> s3: TLC finishes its check
  s4 --> s5: TLC exits or the command kills TLC after Ctrl-C
  s5 --> s2: TLC failed (exit 2) or you pressed Ctrl-C (exit 130)
  s5 --> s6: TLC passed or found a bug (exit 0 or 1)
  s8 --> s8: TLC finishes its check
  s6 --> s7: the files are in --out
  s7 --> s2: the report is on stdout or printing fails because nobody reads stdout (exit 2)
  s0 --> s8: SIGKILL or a crash ends the command
  classDef mayBreak fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#e8730c,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#b85a06
  class s1 bugPath
  class s2 bugPath
  class s3 bugPath
  class s4 bugPath
  class s5 bugPath
  class s6 bugPath
  class s7 bugPath
  class s8 bugPath
  class s8 repeats
  class s9 mayBreak
  class s9 bugPath
